<text >GG_Background:A string in the xdot format specifying an arbitrary background
GG_Bb:Bounding box of drawing in points
GG_Beautify:Whether to draw leaf nodes uniformly in a circle around the root node in sfdp
GG_Bgcolor:Canvas background color
GG_Center:Whether to center the drawing in the output canvas
GG_Charset:Character encoding used when interpreting string input as a text label
GG_Class:Classnames to attach to the node, edge, graph, or cluster&apos;s SVG element
GG_Clusterrank:Mode used for handling clusters
GG_Colorscheme:A color scheme namespace: the context for interpreting color names
GG_Comment:Comments are inserted into output
GG_Compound:If true, allow edges between clusters
GG_Concentrate:If true, use edge concentrators
GG_Damping:Factor damping force motions
GG_Defaultdist:The distance between nodes in separate connected components
GG_Dim:Set the number of dimensions used for the layout
GG_Dimen:Set the number of dimensions used for rendering
GG_Diredgeconstraints:Whether to constrain most edges to point downwards
GG_Dpi:Specifies the expected number of pixels per inch on a display device
GG_Epsilon:Terminating condition
GG_Esep:Margin used around polygons for purposes of spline edge routing
GG_Fontcolor:Color used for text
GG_Fontname:Font used for text
GG_Fontnames:Allows user control of how basic fontnames are represented in SVG output
GG_Fontpath:Directory list used by libgd to search for bitmap fonts
GG_Fontsize:Font size, in points, used for text
GG_Forcelabels:Whether to force placement of all xlabels, even if overlapping
GG_Gradientangle:If a gradient fill is being used, this determines the angle of the fill
GG_Href:Synonym for URL
GG_Id:Identifier for graph objects
GG_Imagepath:A list of directories in which to look for image files
GG_Inputscale:Scales the input positions to convert between length units
GG_K:Spring constant used in virtual physical model
GG_Label:Text label attached to objects
GG_Label_Scheme:Whether to treat a node whose name has the form |edgelabel|* as a special node representing an edge label
GG_Labeljust:Justification for graph &amp; cluster labels
GG_Labelloc:Vertical placement of labels for nodes, root graphs and clusters
GG_Landscape:If true, the graph is rendered in landscape mode
GG_Layerlistsep:The separator characters used to split attributes of type layerRange into a list of ranges
GG_Layers:A linearly ordered list of layer names attached to the graph
GG_Layerselect:Selects a list of layers to be emitted
GG_Layersep:The separator characters for splitting the layers attribute into a list of layer names
GG_Layout:Which layout engine to use
GG_Levels:Number of levels allowed in the multilevel scheme
GG_Levelsgap:strictness of neato level constraints
GG_Lheight:Height of graph or cluster label, in inches
GG_Linelength:How long strings should get before overflowing to next line, for text output
GG_Lp:Label center position
GG_Lwidth:Width of graph or cluster label, in inches
GG_Margin:For graphs, this sets x and y margins of canvas, in inches
GG_Maxiter:Sets the number of iterations used
GG_Mclimit:Scale factor for mincross (mc) edge crossing minimiser parameters
GG_Mindist:Specifies the minimum separation between all nodes
GG_Mode:Technique for optimizing the layout
GG_Model:Specifies how the distance matrix is computed for the input graph
GG_Newrank:Whether to use a single global ranking, ignoring clusters
GG_Nodesep:In dot, nodesep specifies the minimum space between two adjacent nodes in the same rank, in inches
GG_Nojustify:Whether to justify multiline text vs the previous text line (rather than the side of the container)
GG_Normalize:normalizes coordinates of final layout
GG_Notranslate:Whether to avoid translating layout to the origin point
GG_Nslimit:Sets number of iterations in network simplex applications
GG_Nslimit1:Sets number of iterations in network simplex applications
GG_Oneblock:Whether to draw circo graphs around one circle
GG_Ordering:Constrains the left-to-right ordering of node edges
GG_Orientation:node shape rotation angle, or graph orientation
GG_Outputorder:Specify order in which nodes and edges are drawn
GG_Overlap:Determines if and how node overlaps should be removed
GG_Overlap_Scaling:Scale layout by factor, to reduce node overlap
GG_Overlap_Shrink:Whether the overlap removal algorithm should perform a compression pass to reduce the size of the layout
GG_Pack:Whether each connected component of the graph should be laid out separately, and then the graphs packed together
GG_Packmode:How connected components should be packed
GG_Pad:Inches to extend the drawing area around the minimal area needed to draw the graph
GG_Page:Width and height of output pages, in inches
GG_Pagedir:The order in which pages are emitted
GG_Quadtree:Quadtree scheme to use
GG_Quantum:If quantum &gt; 0.0, node label dimensions will be rounded to integral multiples of the quantum
GG_Rankdir:Sets direction of graph layout
GG_Ranksep:Specifies separation between ranks
GG_Ratio:Sets the aspect ratio (drawing height/drawing width) for the drawing
GG_Remincross:If there are multiple clusters, whether to run edge crossing minimization a second time
GG_Repulsiveforce:The power of the repulsive force used in an extended Fruchterman-Reingold
GG_Resolution:Synonym for dpi
GG_Root:Specifies nodes to be used as the center of the layout
GG_Rotate:If rotate=90, sets drawing orientation to landscape
GG_Rotation:Rotates the final layout counter-clockwise by the specified number of degrees
GG_Scale:Scales layout by the given factor after the initial layout
GG_Searchsize:During network simplex, the maximum number of edges with negative cut values to search when looking for an edge with minimum cut value
GG_Sep:Margin to leave around nodes when removing node overlap
GG_Showboxes:Print guide boxes for debugging
GG_Size:Maximum width and height of drawing, in inches
GG_Smoothing:Specifies a post-processing step used to smooth out an uneven distribution of nodes
GG_Sortv:Sort order of graph components for ordering packmode packing
GG_Splines:Controls how, and if, edges are represented
GG_Start:Parameter used to determine the initial layout of nodes
GG_Style:Set style information for components of the graph
GG_Stylesheet:A URL or pathname specifying an XML style sheet, used in SVG output
GG_Target:If the object has a URL, this attribute determines which window of the browser is used for the URL
GG_Tbbalance:Which rank to move floating (loose) nodes to
GG_Tooltip:Tooltip (mouse hover text) attached to the node, edge, cluster, or graph
GG_Truecolor:Whether internal bitmap rendering relies on a truecolor color model or uses
GG_Url:Hyperlinks incorporated into device-dependent output
GG_Viewport:Clipping window on final drawing
GG_Voro_Margin:Tuning margin of Voronoi technique
GG_Xdotversion:Determines the version of xdot used in output
