<text >GC_Area:Indicates the preferred area for a node or empty cluster
GC_Bb:Bounding box of drawing in points
GC_Bgcolor:Canvas background color
GC_Class:Classnames to attach to the node, edge, graph, or cluster&apos;s SVG element
GC_Cluster:Whether the subgraph is a cluster
GC_Color:Basic drawing color for graphics, not text
GC_Colorscheme:A color scheme namespace: the context for interpreting color names
GC_Fillcolor:Color used to fill the background of a node or cluster
GC_Fontcolor:Color used for text
GC_Fontname:Font used for text
GC_Fontsize:Font size, in points, used for text
GC_Gradientangle:If a gradient fill is being used, this determines the angle of the fill
GC_Href:Synonym for URL
GC_Id:Identifier for graph objects
GC_K:Spring constant used in virtual physical model
GC_Label:Text label attached to objects
GC_Labeljust:Justification for graph &amp; cluster labels
GC_Labelloc:Vertical placement of labels for nodes, root graphs and clusters
GC_Layer:Specifies layers in which the node, edge or cluster is present
GC_Lheight:Height of graph or cluster label, in inches
GC_Lp:Label center position
GC_Lwidth:Width of graph or cluster label, in inches
GC_Margin:For graphs, this sets x and y margins of canvas, in inches
GC_Nojustify:Whether to justify multiline text vs the previous text line (rather than the side of the container)
GC_Pencolor:Color used to draw the bounding box around a cluster
GC_Penwidth:Specifies the width of the pen, in points, used to draw lines and curves
GC_Peripheries:Set number of peripheries used in polygonal shapes and cluster boundaries
GC_Sortv:Sort order of graph components for ordering packmode packing
GC_Style:Set style information for components of the graph
GC_Target:If the object has a URL, this attribute determines which window of the browser is used for the URL
GC_Tooltip:Tooltip (mouse hover text) attached to the node, edge, cluster, or graph
GC_Url:Hyperlinks incorporated into device-dependent output
</text>
