<item ID="1767291167" Creator="Chuck Wade" >
<attribute name="Badge" >manage</attribute>
<attribute name="Color" >#009193</attribute>
<attribute name="Created" >2025-01-17T12:55:50+09:00</attribute>
<attribute name="DisplayedAttributes" >Creator;Created;Modified;ID;ChildCount;Reflected_Notes;Reflected_LinkTypes;DiagramAttributesReflection;PlainLinkCount;InboundLinkCount;OutboundLinkCount;RuleDisabled;EdictDisabled</attribute>
<attribute name="DominantLanguage" >en</attribute>
<attribute name="Edict" >if(!$IsPrototype&amp;$Prototype=&quot;Diagram&quot;)
{ // Copy attributes from Reflected Notes to Reflections 
  UpdateDiagramReflections(this); 
  // Re-create all links between Reflection Objects
  UpdateDiagramLinks(this);
};
</attribute>
<attribute name="EdictDisabled" >false</attribute>
<attribute name="IsPrototype" >true</attribute>
<attribute name="Modified" >2025-04-16T21:17:13+09:00</attribute>
<attribute name="NLNames" >Diagram;Shape</attribute>
<attribute name="NLOrganizations" >NameLeading</attribute>
<attribute name="Name" >Diagram</attribute>
<attribute name="NeverComposite" >true</attribute>
<attribute name="OnAdd" >// Reflection Objects should already have their $Prototype set
// However, ad hoc additions of notes and adornments in a Diagram
// will not have prototype assignments, so these are made here.
if($Prototype!=&quot;Reflection Object&quot;)
{ if($IsAdornment)
  { $Prototype=&quot;Diagram Adornment&quot;;
  } else 
  { $Prototype=&quot;Diagram Object&quot;;
  };
};
// Every child note of a Diagram Container needs this absolute 
// reference to its parent to allow updating of reflections
// and other [future] diagram maintenance procedures.
$Diagram_ID=$ID(parent);
// Setting $Text is for debugging purposes; it can be removed.
$Text=$Text.paragraph(0).trim;
$Text+=&quot;Path to reflected note: &quot;+$Path; </attribute>
<attribute name="OnRemove" >action($Text(&quot;/Hints/OnRemove «Diagram Object Note»&quot;));</attribute>
<attribute name="OnVisit" >linkTo(cover,&quot;Diagram←Note&quot;); linkTo(cover,&quot;Diagram_Reflection→Note&quot;);
unlinkTo(cover,&quot;Diagram←Note&quot;); unlinkTo(cover,&quot;Diagram_Reflection→Note&quot;);</attribute>
<attribute name="PrototypeBequeathsChildren" >false</attribute>
<attribute name="Rule" >if(!$IsPrototype&amp;$Prototype=&quot;Diagram&quot;)
{ // Copy attributes from Reflected Notes to Reflections 
  UpdateDiagramReflections(this); 
  // Re-create all links between Reflection Objects
  UpdateDiagramLinks(this);
};
</attribute>
<attribute name="RuleDisabled" >true</attribute>
<attribute name="SafePath" >/Prototypes/Diagram</attribute>
<attribute name="ScreenHeight" >23</attribute>
<attribute name="ScreenWidth" >679</attribute>
<attribute name="SelectionCount" >186</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiment" >-0.6500000127</attribute>
<attribute name="Sentiments" >0.2;-0.6;-0.6;-1;-1;-1;0;-0.8;-0.6;-0.8;-1;-0.8;-0.6;-0.6;-0.4;-0.6;-0.6;-1;-0.6;-0.6</attribute>
<attribute name="URL" >https://acrobatfaq.com/atbref10/index/Automating_Tinderbox/Coding/Links/Link_Types.html</attribute>
<attribute name="Xpos" >421</attribute>
<attribute name="Ypos" >13.5</attribute>
<text > 
Prototype for Diagram Views 
The children of a Container set to this Prototype will be the objects that are included in the Diagram when presented in Map View. For objects that will reflect other notes in the document, the “Reflection Object” Prototype will be assigned.  The Prototype “Diagram Object” will be used for children that exist only as objects to be drawn in the Diagram. Similarly, adornments will be assigned the “Diagram Adornment” object.
When a link of type “Diagram←Note” is created between any note in the document and a Diagram Container, then action code will be invoked to create a Reflection Object child of the container, and a link of type “Diagram_Reflection→Note” will be created from this new child back to the original source note. This allows a source reflected note to find all reflection instances in Diagram Containers.
Note that Diagram Containers are not expected to have grandchildren. This is so that all diagram objects will be at the same level, and consequently will be displayed in Map view.

Terminology:
	•	Diagram A visual layout utilizing Map View, but with a subset of notes from the main document that are decoupled from the document structure, and where notes are shown in the diagram in a way that is independent of the way these notes appear elsewhere. Typically, “block diagrams” will be created using these methods.
	•	Diagram Container A container that collects the objects to be displayed in a diagram, including notes from anywhere in the overall document as well as new objects distinct to the diagram. The “Diagram” Prototype must be used for Diagram Containers.
	•	Reflected Note The original source note that will be reflected into the Diagram. 
	•	Reflection Object A note residing within a Diagram Container that is linked to an original source Reflected note and that mirrors many appearance-oriented aspects of the original, including outbound links that go to other Reflection Objects in the same Diagram Container.
	•	Reflection Link A replication of any outbound links from the Reflected note that connect to other notes in the document that are also reflected into the same diagram.
	•	Reflected Link Types The $Reflected_LinkTypes attribute defines a set of link types that are allowed to be reflected into the diagram. Any user-defined link types that should be included in a diagram need to be added to this attribute for the relevant Diagram Container. Alternatively, the default value assignment for Reflected_LinkTypes can be edited via the Inspector.
	•	Reflection Attributes  $DiagramAttributeReflection is a set of attribute names (without the ‘$’) that will be copied from the Reflected Note to the corresponding Reflection Object. This is maintained in the Diagram Container and serves as the default for all Reflection Objects in the Diagram. However, if  $DiagramAttributeReflection is defined for any Reflection Object, then that local instance will be used to determine which attributes are reflected to that specific Reflection Object.
	•	Reflection Local Attributes If $DiagramReflectionLocals is defined for a Reflection Object, then it must be a set of attribute names (without the ‘$’) that will not be copied (reflected) from the original Reflected Note.  This allows each Reflection Object to have its own appearance without altering the original Reflected Note. 
Usage Notes:
	1.	When an object (note or adornment) is added to a Diagram Container, OnAdd action code will set the $Prototype to either “Diagram Object” or “Diagram Adornment.” Since adding “Reflection Object” notes to a Diagram Container is handled by Link Action code, the OnAdd also checks the $Prototype, and will not modify it if it is already set to “Reflection Object.” In addition, the OnAdd will set “$Diagram_ID” to the $ID of the Diagram Container.
	2.	When a Reflection Object child note is removed from the Diagram Container, OnRemove action code stored as:      /Hints/Library/Remove Diagram Object Note will be executed to handle disconnecting the object from the Diagram Container (i.e., removing associated entry in $Reflected_Notes dictionary) as well as the link to the original source note. This OnRemove also handles any other object type that is either moved out of the Diagram Container or deleted.
	3.	An Edict is defined so that the diagram is periodically updated to reflect changes in original notes or links that are reflected into the diagram. 
	4.	The Default $Reflected_LinkTypes set comprises : [agree;clarify;disagree;example;exception;note;response;update]
	5.	Default appearance-related attributes to be reflected from an original source note to a Reflection Object note include:  [AccentColor;Badge;BadgeMonochrome;BadgeSize;Border;BorderBevel;BorderColor;BorderDash;CaptionAlignment;CaptionColor;CaptionFont;CaptionOpacity;CaptionSize;Color;Flags;Opacity;Pattern;PlotColor;Shadow;ShadowBlur;ShadowColor;ShadowDistance;Shape;Caption;ClusterTerms;Subtitle;Base;Bend;Direction;NameAlignment;NameBold;NameColor;NameFont;NameLeading;NameOpacity;NameStrike;NameVerticalAlignment;Stripe;StripeColor;SubtitleColor;SubtitleOpacity;SubtitleSize;Tip;TitleOpacity;TextBackgroundColor]</text>
